invariant: INV-41
file: rsa_mont64.h
catches: rsa_equiv_test_sum
reason: the sum form of rsa_mont64_mul_add_add, which gcc reads, leaves
  out b, the carry in from the word below, so every word past the first
  of a loop loses the carry of the word before it.
  bin/rsa_equiv_test_sum runs that form under any compiler and compares
  the bytes with the 32-bit arm's.

--- old
    ct_u128 value = ct_mul128(x, y) + a + b;
--- new
    (void)b;
    ct_u128 value = ct_mul128(x, y) + a;
